1|0@vaporents^1440199996#cub96r4:BongRipsPalin$:I'm not the biggest Flowermate fan. They work and they're far from being one of the worst starter vapes, but I prefer the Xmax V2 Pro with the water pipe adapter for that price range. I just think it hits a bit better, and using common, easily swappable batteries is a plus. If you go closer to that $200 point, I'd go for the Air or Goboof Alfa for portable. They'll produce denser, tastier vapor than the cheap, intro kind of units. For desktop, I love my Rise for groups, but I never hit it alone. It's not bad, but it's just not as efficient that way and it tends to be overkill for me. The Nano is on the opposite end, being great for one or two but not for groups, and super efficient. I'm picking one up soon for myself, actually. None of the vaporizers you named in the first post would be disappointing, but which works best depends a lot on how you'll be using it most.
