-3|0@vaporents^1440203559#cubb3gu:mflbninja$:I've heard about how awesome e-nails can be. The thing is they're not portable (that I know about). Just between you and me (lol), I take my Muad-Dib and Power Adapter everywhere. I sneak it into certain single-occupant restrooms that have door locks, power outlets and ventilation fans; then I clear a space somewhere and get my workspace going. It's not long before I'm about two dabs in, already putting it away. :p Anyway, I'm not here to change your opinion, just provide more recent information that might help you change your own opinion. I think it's a really awesome vape, partly because it's *not* easy, but rather it's flexible. Whatever you do, it does. You are completely in control of what happens to the herb. It heats up and cools down fast, and you can flip it as needed, like a frying pan for herb. If it's huge, smooth hits you're after, you can get them with the battery easily, as long as your basics are in order, and you stack hits while using temperature regulation of some kind. If you use it in native mode, feel the temperature indirectly, after it expands so it feels a little cooler. If you stack hits into a rig, find a way to see the vapor so you can regulate it to the density you desire. There's a lot to it that people don't know about and I want to direct them to /r/mflb and /r/mflbguide so they can get more out of this vape. Nothing mythical about it, just straightforward advice and help so you can start getting respectable results out of the Launch Box. It doesn't have to be your only vape, but it is definitely worth keeping.
